    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "known-defect",
      "lines": [
        "Known toolchain defect: vite-plugin-css-injected-by-js 4.0.1 in package-lock.json, where the CSS is injected by JavaScript, puts the code that injects the CSS in front of the chunk without shifting its source map, so the map the bundler combines from it loses sources. Here the map of news-main.mjs names 7 of the 15 packages its .license file names, and 2 further chunks show the same.",
        "  The app runs as built; only the map is short, so the frameworks and libraries are read from the .license files instead.",
        "  Fixed in vite-plugin-css-injected-by-js 5.0.0: https://github.com/marco-prontera/vite-plugin-css-injected-by-js/issues/155",
        "  Built in a copy with @nextcloud/vite-config 3.0.0-beta.1, vite 8.3.5 (vite-plugin-css-injected-by-js 5.0.3), the map of shared-Dyc2uNef.chunk.mjs names 40 of the 42 packages its .license file names: fixed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "ok",
      "id": "source-maps",
      "lines": [
        "Every delivered file in js carries a source map, so every byte can be charged to the package and the module it came from."
      ]
